@@ -243,7 +243,9 @@ Canvas cloth rendered from a source picture on a 7px weave cell: cells above .62
 The hero network arrives before anything else: it develops out of scattered dots, from the middle of the network outwards, over two seconds (each cell takes its moment from its distance to the network's centre plus a stable random offset, on an ease-out curve). Each newly woven cell is Crown Pearl for 520ms before it cools to lilac. The name and lede rise in halfway through, and the output labels fade in once the network is whole. It runs on touch too; reduced motion gets the finished cloth with everything in place.
 
 ### The field (signature)
-One halftone light lies behind the whole page instead of a separate one per chapter. Its warp dots sit on the same 6px grid as the hero and scroll with the page; the light glides across them, holding through each chapter and easing to the next chapter's spot over the last half of the one before, always kept out of the reading column. It rises from the bottom right as the hero leaves. While you scroll fast the lit dots draw out into short weft floats and settle back into dots when you stop; on fine pointers the dots lift near the cursor on the lit side of the page. Chapters are no longer divided by hairlines: a short Regent Violet float before each chapter label marks the change instead. Reduced motion gets the same light, placed without easing, floats or lift.
+One night sky lies behind the whole page, woven into the cloth. Its warp dots sit on the same 6px grid as the hero and scroll with the page. Each chapter has its own constellation, drawn from real star positions and magnitudes (`assets/data/constellations.js`) and projected as it sits in the sky, north up: Orion for About, Auriga the charioteer for Work, Lyra (Vega, the weaver's star) for Skills, Cassiopeia for Education, the Plough for Experience and Ursa Minor, ending on Polaris, for Contact. The hero has its own picture, so its sky stays dark. Stars are woven by the loom's own rule: a core of weft floats above .62 tone, a halo of halftone dots sized by tone, Regent Violet in the shade and Court Lilac in the body; brighter stars are bigger, and only the cores of the brightest reach Crown Pearl (The Thread Light Rule: brightness is magnitude). Lines between stars are dotted Regent Violet threads.
+
+Scroll drives it. As a chapter arrives its stars light brightest first, then its lines draw from star to star; just before the next chapter it unweaves in reverse and the next constellation takes its place, with no gap and no overlap. The sky turns 7 degrees through each chapter, and nothing moves while the page is still. The constellation sits in the right margin at up to 380px; below 860px it shrinks to the top right corner and stays dots only. While you scroll fast the lit dots draw out into short weft floats; on fine pointers the lit cloth lifts near the cursor, and the cursor never adds light of its own. Chapters are not divided by hairlines: a short Regent Violet float before each chapter label marks the change instead. Reduced motion gets each constellation whole and still.
 
 ### The live network (signature)
 After the entry finishes, the hero network replays one real lap of the all-rounder on the technical track (`ALL_ROUNDER.lap`: 11 recorded sensor inputs and the 3 outputs, sampled at 15 Hz from the game). Each frame runs the inputs through the real weights and biases (tanh, 11 → 8 → 3), so nothing is invented: brightness is the signal a connection is actually carrying (The Thread Light Rule).
